  "promptDocsUrl": "https://gitee.com/gzxx-2025/aid-studio/blob/master/doc/%E6%8F%90%E7%A4%BA%E8%AF%8D%E5%BC%80%E5%8F%91%E6%8C%87%E5%8D%97.md",
  "publishedAt": "2026-09-16 00:11:56",
  "releaseNotes": "# AID v2.1.5\n\n## 中文更新说明\n\n### 模型、计费与任务安全\n\n- GPT-5.6 的展示名称更新为 GPT-5.6 Sol，平台稳定编码继续使用 `gpt-5.6`，真实上游模型统一为 `gpt-5.6-sol`，既有 Skill 与业务引用无需修改。\n- GPT-5.6 Sol 的内置计费基线更新为不超过 272K 与超过 272K 两档，覆盖输入、缓存读取、缓存写入、可见输出和推理 Token；迁移只修正已知旧内置价格，不覆盖站长自定义 SKU。\n- 文本模型失败结算统一依据真实调用证据：请求未发送，或上游明确最终拒绝且没有产生用量时全额解冻；已返回用量按实际用量结算；超时、断链、私有状态码、5xx 或结果不确定时继续保守结算。\n- OpenAI 兼容（含 DeepSeek）、Gemini 与 TokenDance 文本协议会在预冻结和排队提交前校验密钥、地址及端点，避免本地配置错误进入可能计费边界。\n\n### Web 用户端\n\n- 新增账号安全设置中心，并优化账号设置表单的间距、操作按钮和信息层级。\n- 修复素材提示词编辑、登录反馈、生成后提示词保留、弹窗提示词格式回显及确认弹窗布局问题。\n- 修复无需生成分镜图的创作模式仍会打开分镜图编辑弹窗的问题；跨步骤返回时会按当前创作模式决定是否打开编辑器。\n\n### 分镜生成与任务恢复\n\n- 修复包括 Agnes 在内的视频模型及分镜图片批量任务在部分失败后续生时只统计本轮镜头的问题；现在会按原批次完整镜头范围汇总历史成功与本轮结果，避免产物已全部落库但父任务仍无法成功收口并被超时回收。\n- 批量生成部分失败时保留每一项的安全错误提示，客户端优先展示 `failedItems[].userMessage`，缺失时再回退到任务级 `errorMessage`。\n\n### 数据库与升级说明\n\n- 已有环境按迁移顺序执行 `sql/v2.1.5.sql`。脚本兼容 MySQL 5.7、可重复执行，并为早期安装链补齐 GPT-5.6 Sol 缺失的结构化能力、协议绑定和模型别名。\n- 已在 MySQL 5.7.44 隔离库从 `v1.0.0-beta.1` 连续执行全部正式增量到 `v2.1.5`，整条迁移链重复执行两遍均成功；当前初始化基线要求的表、字段、索引、公共配置键和公开模型缺失数均为 0。\n- 自定义模型价格、协议路由、启停状态、密钥、网关、倍率与模型池不会被本次迁移覆盖。正式渠道最低一键直升版本继续为 `v1.0.0-beta.1`。\n- 本版本包含服务端和 Web 用户端变更；后台管理端代码没有变化。升级前仍请备份数据库、部署配置、证书和用户媒体目录。\n\n### 开源文档\n\n- README 鸣谢新增 Linux.do 社区，并明确交流群仅用于开源交流与技术支持，不含广告及隐形消费。\n- 重构 README 中英双语入口和产品首屏，补齐英文部署、首次创作、维护指南、贡献指南、安全说明、支持说明、社区准则与 Issue/PR 模板。\n- 增加服务端与后台管理端 GitHub Actions 自动构建门禁；安装示例优先使用正式渠道，第三方归属统一收录于 NOTICE，并保留标准 MIT 许可。\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n### Models, Billing, and Task Safety\n\n- GPT-5.6 is now displayed as GPT-5.6 Sol. The stable platform code remains `gpt-5.6`, while the upstream model is normalized to `gpt-5.6-sol`, so existing Skills and business references remain compatible.\n- The built-in GPT-5.6 Sol billing baseline now has separate tiers for contexts up to 272K and above 272K, covering input, cache reads, cache writes, visible output, and reasoning tokens. The migration updates only recognized legacy built-in prices and preserves administrator-defined SKUs.\n- Text failure settlement now follows provider-independent call evidence: requests that were never sent, or explicit final refusals with no usage, are fully released; reported usage is settled as reported; timeouts, disconnects, private status codes, 5xx responses, and uncertain outcomes remain conservatively settled.\n- OpenAI-compatible providers (including DeepSeek), Gemini, and TokenDance validate credentials, endpoints, and base URLs before reservation and again before queued submission, preventing local configuration errors from entering a potentially billable boundary.\n\n### Web Client\n\n- Added an account security settings center and refined spacing, action hierarchy, and visual structure in account settings.\n- Fixed media prompt editing, login feedback, prompt retention after generation, prompt formatting in dialogs, and confirmation-dialog layout.\n- Fixed image-editor dialogs opening in creation modes that do not generate storyboard images. Cross-step navigation now respects the active creation mode.\n\n### Storyboard Generation and Task Recovery\n\n- Fixed resumed batch storyboard image and video tasks, including Agnes-backed video jobs, counting only the current retry instead of the complete original shot range. Historical successes and current results now converge into one authoritative terminal summary.\n- Partial batch failures preserve item-level safe error messages. Clients should prefer `failedItems[].userMessage` and fall back to the task-level `errorMessage` only when needed.\n\n### Database and Upgrade Notes\n\n- Existing installations apply `sql/v2.1.5.sql` in migration order. The script is MySQL 5.7 compatible and idempotent, and it restores missing structured capability, protocol binding, and model alias records for GPT-5.6 Sol on early installation chains.\n- The complete versioned migration chain from `v1.0.0-beta.1` through `v2.1.5` was executed twice on an isolated MySQL 5.7.44 instance. No required current-baseline tables, columns, indexes, public configuration keys, or public models were missing afterward.\n- Custom model pricing, protocol routes, enablement, credentials, gateways, multipliers, and model-pool assignments are preserved. The stable one-click upgrade floor remains `v1.0.0-beta.1`.\n- This release changes the server and Web client; the admin application source is unchanged. Back up the database, deployment configuration, certificates, and user media before upgrading.\n\n### Open-source Documentation\n\n- Added the Linux.do community to README acknowledgements and clarified that the community group is dedicated to open-source discussion and technical support, without advertising or hidden charges.\n- Reworked the bilingual README entry and product hero, and added English deployment, first-creation, maintenance, contribution, security, support, community, Issue, and pull-request guidance.\n- Added GitHub Actions build gates for the backend and admin application. Installation examples now prefer the stable channel, third-party attribution is centralized in NOTICE, and the standard MIT license is retained.",
